      "content": "Even if your blood sugar was only slightly elevated at 180 mg/dL, it's still beneficial to monitor it closely, especially when introducing a new supplement into your regimen. Your symptoms, however, indicate an increasingly problematic response. You are not overreacting; these are potential signs of an imbalance or a strong reaction to the new supplement that could exacerbate your diabetes. Dehydration from increased urination, excessive thirst, and a reliance on Gatorade can lead to a dangerous electrolyte imbalance. It’s critical to seek medical advice rather than self-managing, as making the right choices now can prevent more serious and costly health issues later on. I strongly encourage you to schedule an appointment with your healthcare provider or visit urgent care to assess the situation promptly. Sharing these concerns with a medical professional will ensure you receive the correct guidance and treatment.",
